---
interface Props {
  heading?: string | null;
}
const { heading = 'Which replacement method fits the opening?' } = Astro.props;
---
<figure class="compare-diagram">
  {heading && <figcaption class="diagram-heading">{heading}</figcaption>}
  <p class="diagram-intro">The important question is what happens to the <strong>existing frame</strong>. Sound frame? Keep it. Damaged or out of square? Open the wall back up.</p>

  <div class="compare-grid">
    <article class="compare-card compare-card-keep">
      <header>
        <span class="compare-badge">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Insert replacement</h3>
          <p>Keep the existing frame.</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <svg class="compare-svg" viewBox="0 0 520 360" role="img" aria-label="Insert replacement cross-section. The existing window frame remains in the wall and a smaller new window is fitted inside it.">
        <defs>
          <marker id="arrow-keep" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 Z" class="arrow-head" /></marker>
        </defs>
        <rect x="32" y="48" width="456" height="42" rx="6" class="wall-siding" />
        <rect x="32" y="90" width="456" height="34" class="wall-wrap" />
        <rect x="32" y="124" width="82" height="188" class="wall-stud" />
        <rect x="406" y="124" width="82" height="188" class="wall-stud" />
        <rect x="114" y="124" width="54" height="188" rx="5" class="frame-kept" />
        <rect x="352" y="124" width="54" height="188" rx="5" class="frame-kept" />
        <rect x="168" y="140" width="184" height="156" rx="4" class="new-unit" />
        <line x1="260" y1="140" x2="260" y2="296" class="unit-line" />
        <rect x="32" y="312" width="456" height="16" rx="4" class="interior" />

        <line x1="142" y1="116" x2="142" y2="72" class="leader keep-leader" marker-end="url(#arrow-keep)" />
        <text x="142" y="44" class="callout callout-strong">EXISTING FRAME STAYS</text>

        <line x1="260" y1="324" x2="260" y2="342" class="leader" />
        <text x="260" y="357" class="caption center">new unit fits inside the old frame</text>

        <text x="73" y="220" class="wall-label">WALL</text>
        <text x="445" y="220" class="wall-label">WALL</text>
        <text x="260" y="220" class="unit-label">NEW WINDOW</text>
      </svg>

      <ul class="compare-points">
        <li><strong>Keeps:</strong> existing frame, much of the interior/exterior finish</li>
        <li><strong>Best when:</strong> the opening is sound and square</li>
        <li><strong>Usually means:</strong> less disturbance and a simpler install</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="verdict verdict-keep"><strong>Think:</strong> upgrade the window without rebuilding the opening.</div>
    </article>

    <article class="compare-card compare-card-remove">
      <header>
        <span class="compare-badge">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Full-frame replacement</h3>
          <p>Remove the old frame to the rough opening.</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <svg class="compare-svg" viewBox="0 0 520 360" role="img" aria-label="Full-frame replacement cross-section. The old frame is removed to the rough opening, the opening is re-flashed, and the new window is installed to the wall structure.">
        <defs>
          <marker id="arrow-remove" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 Z" class="arrow-head" /></marker>
        </defs>
        <rect x="32" y="48" width="456" height="42" rx="6" class="wall-siding" />
        <rect x="32" y="90" width="456" height="34" class="wall-wrap" />
        <rect x="32" y="124" width="82" height="188" class="wall-stud" />
        <rect x="406" y="124" width="82" height="188" class="wall-stud" />
        <rect x="114" y="124" width="54" height="188" rx="5" class="frame-removed" />
        <rect x="352" y="124" width="54" height="188" rx="5" class="frame-removed" />
        <path d="M114 124 V108 H168" class="flashing" />
        <path d="M406 124 V108 H352" class="flashing" />
        <rect x="114" y="140" width="292" height="156" rx="4" class="new-unit" />
        <line x1="260" y1="140" x2="260" y2="296" class="unit-line" />
        <line x1="114" y1="140" x2="96" y2="140" class="fin" />
        <line x1="406" y1="140" x2="424" y2="140" class="fin" />
        <rect x="32" y="312" width="456" height="16" rx="4" class="interior" />

        <line x1="141" y1="116" x2="90" y2="72" class="leader remove-leader" marker-end="url(#arrow-remove)" />
        <text x="48" y="44" class="callout callout-strong">OLD FRAME COMES OUT</text>
        <line x1="260" y1="110" x2="260" y2="76" class="leader" marker-end="url(#arrow-remove)" />
        <text x="260" y="61" class="caption center">opening is re-flashed</text>

        <text x="73" y="220" class="wall-label">WALL</text>
        <text x="445" y="220" class="wall-label">WALL</text>
        <text x="260" y="220" class="unit-label">NEW WINDOW</text>
      </svg>

      <ul class="compare-points">
        <li><strong>Keeps:</strong> the rough opening and structural framing</li>
        <li><strong>Best when:</strong> the old frame is rotten, damaged, or out of square</li>
        <li><strong>Usually means:</strong> more trim/siding work and a deeper inspection</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="verdict verdict-remove"><strong>Think:</strong> rebuild the opening so the new window starts from a sound base.</div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="diagram-takeaway"><strong>The decision is made at the house.</strong> A photo can suggest a method; the opening condition determines it.</div>
</figure>

<style>
  .compare-diagram { margin: 0; }
  .diagram-heading { display: block; margin: 0 0 var(--space-2xs); font-size: var(--step-2); font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display); line-height: var(--leading-display); }
  .diagram-intro { margin: 0 0 var(--space-l); max-width: 64ch; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .compare-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-m); }
  .compare-card { padding: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.4rem); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--paper-raised); }
  .compare-card header { display: flex; gap: var(--space-s); align-items: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-s); }
  .compare-card header h3 { margin: 0 0 0.15rem; font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .compare-card header p { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .compare-badge { flex: none; width: 2.5rem; height: 2.5rem; display: grid; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); font-size: var(--step--2); font-weight: 700; }
  .compare-card-keep .compare-badge { background: var(--accent); }
  .compare-card-remove .compare-badge { background: var(--danger); }
  .compare-svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; background: var(--paper-sunk); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  .wall-siding { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 15%, transparent); }
  .wall-wrap { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 8%, transparent); stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 22%, transparent); stroke-width: 1; }
  .wall-stud { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 14%, transparent); }
  .interior { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 21%, transparent); }
  .frame-kept { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, transparent); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 3; }
  .frame-removed { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 10%, transparent); stroke: var(--danger); stroke-width: 2.5; stroke-dasharray: 9 7; }
  .new-unit { fill: var(--paper-raised); stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 3; }
  .unit-line { stroke: var(--ink-soft); stroke-width: 2; }
  .flashing { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 8; stroke-linecap: square; }
  .fin { stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 4; }
  .leader { stroke: var(--ink-soft); stroke-width: 2.5; fill: none; }
  .keep-leader { stroke: var(--accent); }
  .remove-leader { stroke: var(--danger); }
  .arrow-head { fill: currentColor; }
  .callout { fill: var(--ink); font-family: Outfit, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-anchor: middle; }
  .callout-strong { font-size: 12px; }
  .caption { fill: var(--ink-soft); font-family: Outfit, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 550; }
  .center { text-anchor: middle; }
  .wall-label { fill: var(--ink-faint); font-family: Outfit, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em; text-anchor: middle; }
  .unit-label { fill: var(--ink); font-family: Outfit, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-anchor: middle; }
  .compare-points { margin: var(--space-s) 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: .45rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .compare-points strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .verdict { margin-top: var(--space-s); padding: .7rem .8rem; border-radius: var(--radius); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .verdict-keep { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 10%, transparent); }
  .verdict-remove { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 9%, transparent); }
  .verdict strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .diagram-takeaway { margin-top: var(--space-m); padding: var(--space-s) var(--space-m); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); background: var(--paper-raised); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .diagram-takeaway strong { color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .compare-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
